<title>UK: Sema completes Brit Rail business unit buy.</title>
<headline>Sema completes Brit Rail business unit buy.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-French technology company SEMA Group Plc said on Monday it completed the 27 million stg acquisition of BR Business Systemes Ltd, a company formed to take over British Rail's business service division.</p>
<p>The consideration was paid from existing resources, SEMA said.</p>
<p>At October 12 1996, BR Business Systems had net assets of 13.2 million stg.</p>
<p>The unit's acquisition provides synergies with existing rail systems business, which has provided systems for rail operators in Britain, France, Netherlands and Spain, SEMA said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
